{
  "opening": "This release addresses critical bugs in debug output formatting, result addition logic, and datetime parsing precision, while introducing new warning classes for better diagnostics. It also expands the public API with new interpreter nodes and engine methods for the Tiny language example.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m05",
      "text": "The `parse_tiny` function must utilize the `infix_notation` method and exclude \"op\" results names."
    },
    {
      "id": "m11",
      "text": "The `TinyEngine` class must maintain interpreter state using `TinyFrame` objects and construct executable AST nodes of types such as `AssignStmtNode`, `CallStmtNode`, `DeclStmtNode`, `IfStmtNode`, `MainDeclNode`, `ReadStmtNode`, `RepeatStmtNode`, and `WriteStmtNode`. The module must expose helper functions including `assign_var`, `current_frame`, `declare`, `declare_var`, `eval_expr`, `from_statement_type`, `get`, and `get_type`."
    },
    {
      "id": "m15",
      "text": "The `MainDeclNode` execute method must no longer perform ParseResults to AST conversion; instead, it should rely on `build_contained_statements`. The `execute` method must correctly handle `DeclStmtNode`, `AssignStmtNode`, and `RepeatStmtNode` execution."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18",
      "text": "The `execute` method must support `ReadStmtNode` and `WriteStmtNode` operations within the `RepeatStmtNode` context."
    },
    {
      "id": "m20",
      "text": "The `TinyEngine` must implement `IfStmtNode` execution and support relational operators `<=` and `>=`. The `build_contained_statements` method must be updated to accommodate these changes."
    },
    {
      "id": "m42",
      "text": "The `TinyEngine` class must expose an `initialize_engine` method for separate initialization, and the `main` function must use this refactored approach."
    },
    {
      "id": "m86",
      "text": "No public API changes are required for this change."
    },
    {
      "id": "m99",
      "text": "The library must define and expose `PyparsingWarning` (inheriting from `UserWarning`), `PyparsingDeprecationWarning` (inheriting from `PyparsingWarning` and `DeprecationWarning`), and `PyparsingDiagnosticWarning` (inheriting from `PyparsingWarning`). These warnings must be selectively enableable or disableable without affecting other libraries' warnings."
    },
    {
      "id": "m119",
      "text": "The `pyparsing_common` module must expose the `as_datetime` parse action and the `iso8601_date_validated` and `iso8601_datetime_validated` expressions. The `version_info` attribute must be available."
    },
    {
      "id": "m151",
      "text": "The docstring for `TinyNode.from_statement_type` must be corrected for accuracy."
    },
    {
      "id": "m164",
      "text": "The `pyparsing_common.as_datetime` parse action must correctly scale fractional seconds to microseconds, ensuring that input like \"1997-07-16T19:20:30.45\" yields a microsecond value of 450000 rather than 449."
    },
    {
      "id": "m166",
      "text": "The `version_info` attribute must reflect the inclusion of fixes for `ParseResults.__add__` and `ParseResults.__radd__`."
    },
    {
      "id": "m167",
      "text": "When `pyparsing_common.as_datetime` raises a `ParseException`, it must pass the input string as the position argument (`pstr`) instead of the ParseResults object, preventing secondary TypeErrors during message formatting."
    },
    {
      "id": "m169",
      "text": "The `condition_as_parse_action` function used by `set_debug` must escape control characters in the printed source line to prevent terminal cursor corruption, keeping the caret aligned with the match location."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure all public names listed above are exposed exactly as specified and that the behavioral constraints regarding errors and outputs are strictly met."
}
